From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a headless desk takes emulated input

On a headless desk the only pointer and keyboard are an EIS client's. The
compositor hands each event to the engine, which makes the event a real
device's would and gives it to the shell's window, so the shell and its
lock screen see it. See docs/architecture/A-HEADLESS-DESKTOP.md in the
Domicile repository.

- OzonePlatform::InjectDomicileInput takes a pointer move, button, scroll
  or key, in desk pixels and evdev codes.
- Headless keeps the desk host and, with the desk switch, an xkb layout so
  keys type what the compositor's keymap says.
- With the desk switch, cursors come from Chromium's art and each window
  sets the pointer image the casts draw (DeskCursorImageSource, as DRM's
  DrmCursor does).
- No key repeat.
